# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml — root AI manifest for IDApTIK

## Purpose

IDApTIK is an asymmetric two-player infiltration game (attempt four). Rust owns
deterministic gameplay truth, Elixir/OTP owns multiplayer session life, and
Bevy is the selected graphical frontend.

Read `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, `GOVERNANCE.md`,
`docs/PROJECT-GOVERNANCE-BINDING.adoc`, and
`.machine_readable/descriptiles/STATE.a2ml` before editing.

## Where things live

- `crates/idaptik-core` — engine-agnostic gameplay truth and package loader.
- `crates/idaptik-net` — deterministic delay-lockstep client and resync.
- `crates/idaptik-ffi` — C-ABI surface for non-Rust consumers.
- `crates/idaptik-tui` — playable reference frontend and headless verifier.
- `crates/idaptik-bevy` — selected graphical frontend (ADR-0008).
- sibling `../burble/server/` — Bandit + Phoenix Channels relay; override with
  `IDAPTIK_BURBLE_DIR` when the checkout lives elsewhere.
- `config/` — typed Nickel configuration and negative fixtures.
- `contracts/idaptik/v1/` — game-owned UMS package contract.
- `docs/adr/` — architecture decision records.
- `.machine_readable/descriptiles/` — project state and supporting metadata.
- `.machine_readable/contractiles/` — machine-readable operating contracts.

## Invariants

- Code is AGPL-3.0-or-later, game content is CC-BY-SA-4.0, and the IDApTIK and
  Moletaire names/marks are trademarked. Do not flatten these layers.
- Gameplay truth remains deterministic and independent of Bevy.
- Render-derived state never feeds the simulation.
- The session layer is Bandit + Phoenix Channels, not LiveView.
- Ruby, Python, and JavaScript are not implementation or project-tooling
  languages in this repository.
- UMS consumes IDApTIK-owned versioned packages; IDApTIK does not depend on
  the UMS user interface.
- Contributions use DCO 1.1 and signed-off commits.
